# The launcher's search and the Settings window (0.0.5g): typing in the
# search box finds an application; Settings changes the accent colour (a
# swatch, then any hue from the strip), the wallpaper and the window-border
# effect; the screen resolution changes and changes back, with the desktop
# and the shell still working at each size.
# Coordinates assume the 1280x800 test display and the Settings window
# opening centred (frame at 290,92, 700x560; content origin 291,125; the
# sidebar is 172 wide, cards start at content x=192, their chips at x=208).
bga: display adapter
gui: desktop up at 1280x800
cerberus kernel shell
# Click the taskbar's search box, type, and take the first match with Enter.
!mouseto 150 780
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!key set
!wait 1
!screenshot build/settings-1.png
# Appearance: a custom hue from the strip, then the teal swatch.
!mouseto 720 233
!button left down
!mouse 40 0
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/settings-1b.png
!mouseto 793 199
!button left down
!button left up
# Wallpaper tab: Aurora.
!mouseto 370 193
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 690 220
!button left down
!button left up
# Window borders: the Chase effect, 3 pixels wide.
!mouseto 370 233
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 535 236
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 660 420
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.7
!screenshot build/settings-2.png
# Display: down to 1024x768.
!mouseto 340 273
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 658 198
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 1.5
gui: resolution changed to 1024x768
!screenshot build/settings-3.png
# The terminal still takes input at the new size.
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key ticks
!wait 1
ticks=
# And back up to 1280x800 (the Settings window kept its place).
!mouseto 600 107
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 888 198
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 1.5
gui: resolution changed to 1280x800
!screenshot build/settings-4.png
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key gui
!wait 1
frames
# The same from the keyboard: the shell's `resolution` command.
!key resolution 1440 900
!wait 1.5
gui: resolution changed to 1440x900
!key resolution
!wait 1
resolution: 1440x900
!key resolution 99 99
!wait 1
resolution: this display cannot show 99x99
